    "summary": "Complementary paired movements with independent sets and flexible recovery.",
    "description": "## Who it suits\n\nLifters familiar with controlled technique who prefer complementary, moderate-effort pairings.\n\n## The rotation\n\nFollow the ordered training and recovery positions; they are not fixed weekdays. Add recovery when needed. Prescribed Supersets are real two-member groups. The squat and hinge work stays separate.\n\n## Progression\n\nProgress each exercise independently within its repetition range. Keep roughly three repetitions available; use lighter loads for paired work. No combined Superset strength score is calculated.\n\n## Before you lift\n\nWarm up separately. Alternate paired movements at a controlled pace, then take enough recovery for technique and breathing. Rest guidance is not a timer requirement. Stop when a movement causes pain. These are original, unbranded Body templates.",
